From ea4d39eda19e411b530391212a6ead89d2c57aa7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:24:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 093/112] Filters: every filter param glides to a new value in
 10 ms, whatever sets it, in voices and in the song, kits, tracks

Spec point 8. The LPF's and HPF's cutoff, resonance and morph take a new value through a one-pole on the param's value
(the cutoffs' is their log frequency), time constant 10 ms, advanced once per block by exactly the block's share
(dsp/filter/param_glide.h), so a knob click, a step of automation or a MIDI CC step (~94 cents on the cutoff) becomes
a smooth curve that the per-sample coefficient ramps carry through each block. Voices: Sound::filterGlide, fed by
notifyValueChangeViaLPF() for all six params (knob, automation, MIDI alike, several at once; the cutoffs no longer
take the one-at-a-time param LPF), read by the patcher through getSmoothedPatchedParamValue(), moved on in
doFilterGlide() after each render, ended in startSkippingRendering(). Song, kits, audio tracks:
GlobalEffectable::setupFilterSetConfig() glides the unpatched params (it now gets the block's length); the filter modes
follow the glide (a filter opened all the way switches off when it gets there); renderWithNothingToRender() ends it.
Modulation (envelopes, LFOs, velocity, cables' sources) doesn't go through it. A param that stays put renders exactly
as before (the glide lands on the value, within 2^-20 of the range then exactly, and stops).

tests/filters filter_neutral glide: 63 % after 441 samples (+ up to one block) for blocks of 32 / 60 / 128, exact
landing, no overshoot; a CC step every 10 ms on a kit's LPF: 13 dB less above 2 kHz than taking each step at once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
